---
title: "Experiment design - what is held fixed, what varies"
---
flowchart LR
  subgraph FIXED["Held fixed for every run"]
    direction TB
    gpu["<b>One A10G</b><br/>started once, never re-provisioned"]
    engine["<b>vLLM 0.29</b> - Qwen2.5-0.5B<br/>4 concurrent max, FCFS<br/>prefix caching off"]
    traffic["<b>Same traffic</b><br/>150 requests, ~20/s, seed 0<br/>54% interactive / 26% streaming / 20% batch"]
  end

  subgraph VARIES["The only thing that varies"]
    direction TB
    p1["Accept everything<br/><i>the baseline to beat</i>"]
    p2["Queue-depth limit<br/><i>refuse when 4+ are waiting</i>"]
    p3["Chronos-inspired<br/><i>the paper's test</i>"]
    p4["Chronos-inspired, cautious<br/><i>2x safety margin</i>"]
  end

  out[/"3 repeats each = 12 runs<br/>accepted % · latency · deadlines met"/]

  FIXED --> VARIES --> out

  note["Fair on infrastructure: identical server and traffic throughout.<br/>NOT fair on tuning: the queue-depth knob was set sensibly for this server,<br/>while Chronos runs with a per-step overhead measured on different hardware."]
  out -.-> note

  classDef fixed fill:#ccfbf1,stroke:#0f766e,color:#134e4a,stroke-width:2px
  classDef varies fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#1e40af,color:#1e3a8a,stroke-width:2px
  classDef result fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#b45309,color:#7c2d12,stroke-width:2px
  classDef caveat fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#b91c1c,color:#7f1d1d

  class gpu,engine,traffic fixed
  class p1,p2,p3,p4 varies
  class out result
  class note caveat
